<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Hepburn returns three months after her first visit and twelve weeks after starting propranolol extended-release 60 mg each morning. Her hands are steadier: she can carry a full cup again and signs letters more easily, though writing still tires her hand. The head tremor is about the same. She finished the six-week voice therapy course a month ago and uses breath support and a slightly higher pitch on stage, which steadies sustained notes. She has had no lightheadedness on standing, wheeze, cold hands, unusual tiredness, vivid dreams, or low mood, and no falls. Occupational therapy has not yet been booked. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Medicine</td><td>Propranolol extended-release 60 mg daily for twelve weeks; no side effects</td></tr><tr><td>Tremor</td><td>Hands steadier; head tremor unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>Voice therapy</td><td>Six-week course completed; strategies in use</td></tr><tr><td>Falls</td><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

