    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Essential tremor (G25.0)</content>. Hand tremor improved on propranolol, with TETRAS performance down from 22 to 16 and the daily-living score from 14 to 9. Head tremor unchanged, as is common. Pulse 64 with no side effects. The standing blood pressure was not measured today. [S]<list><item>Continue propranolol extended-release 60 mg each morning; no dose increase, because the pulse is 64 and she is satisfied with the benefit.</item><item>Seated and standing blood pressure at the six-month review.</item><item>Book the occupational therapy evaluation for adaptive aids.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Voice tremor due to essential tremor (R49.8)</content>. Steadier sustained notes after the voice therapy course. [S]<list><item>Keep using the voice strategies.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Tremor rating: TETRAS performance and activities of daily living subscales</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Performance subscale 16, down from 22; daily-living subscale 9, down from 14</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Archimedes spiral drawing and handwriting sample</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Smaller tremor waves in both spirals; handwriting steadier</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Examination for signs beyond tremor (rest tremor, bradykinesia, rigidity, dystonia, ataxia, cognitive change)</td><td>At diagnosis, then yearly or with a change in the tremor</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No new signs; full review by neurology three months ago</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Resting heart rate and seated and 3-minute standing blood pressure</td><td>Every visit on a beta-blocker</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Pulse 64 and seated blood pressure 122/72 mmHg were recorded, but the 3-minute standing blood pressure was not measured, a deviation from the every-visit item after starting a beta-blocker. She has no lightheadedness or falls, and the standing pressure at the six-month review showed no orthostatic drop, so no harm resulted. Corrective action: standing blood pressure is added to the rooming checklist for every visit on propranolol</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Beta-blocker safety: wheeze, slow pulse or heart block, fatigue, cold hands, low mood, hypoglycemia awareness</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No wheeze, fatigue, cold hands, or vivid dreams; pulse 64</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Primidone safety: sedation, unsteadiness, nausea</td><td>Every visit on primidone</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not on primidone; propranolol is working</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Drugs and substances that worsen tremor (beta-agonists, valproate, lithium, antidepressants, excess thyroid hormone, caffeine)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No new medicines; coffee unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fall query, with Timed Up and Go yearly</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Mood (PHQ-9)</td><td>Before a beta-blocker, after starting it, then yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 3 after twelve weeks on propranolol; no depression</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>TSH and basic chemistry to exclude metabolic causes</td><td>Once at diagnosis; again only with a change in the tremor</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Normal at diagnosis; no change in the tremor to repeat them</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Speech-language therapy for voice tremor</td><td>When voice tremor affects speech or work</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Six-week course of 12 sessions completed a month ago</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Occupational therapy for adaptive aids</td><td>When tremor limits daily tasks</td><td>Due</td><td>Not yet booked; to be arranged now</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Botulinum toxin for head or voice tremor</td><td>If head or voice tremor is disabling</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Head tremor does not trouble her; voice steadier</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Referral for focused ultrasound thalamotomy or deep brain stimulation</td><td>If disabling limb tremor persists after adequate trials of propranolol and primidone</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Good response to the first medicine</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Cognitive screen (MoCA)</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>MoCA 28 four months ago</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>AGS Beers Criteria medication review</td><td>Yearly from age 65</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Reviewed three months ago; no new medicines</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Advance care planning and goals of care</td><td>At least yearly from 65</td><td>Due</td><td>At the annual wellness visit in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Vaccination status (influenza, pneumococcal, zoster, COVID-19, Tdap)</td><td>Yearly, per the CDC schedule</td><td>Due</td><td>At the annual wellness visit</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Less hand tremor with daily tasks on a well-tolerated medicine, with resting heart rate 55 or above and no lightheadedness, by the three-month review. Outcome by 1980-05-05: TETRAS performance subscale fell from 22 to 16 and the activities of daily living subscale from 14 to 9 on propranolol; heart rate 64; no lightheadedness or falls [S]</item><item>Complete a course of voice therapy and use the strategies on stage. Outcome by 1980-05-05: Six-week course completed; steadier sustained notes with breath support and a slightly higher pitch [S]</item><item>Use adaptive aids for eating, drinking, and writing. In progress; target 1980-10-06 [S]</item><item>Name a health care agent and record her goals of care by the annual wellness visit. In progress; target 1980-10-06 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Evidence-based guideline update: treatment of essential tremor: report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology (2011); Practice parameter: therapies for essential tremor: report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology (2005); Consensus Statement on the classification of tremors, from the task force on tremor of the International Parkinson and Movement Disorder Society (2018); MDS evidence-based review of treatments for essential tremor (2019); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, general items for older adults (no essential tremor monograph) (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Six-month tremor review in three months, with seated and standing blood pressure. Occupational therapy to be booked. Next scheduled visit 1980-08-04: six-month tremor review. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
